hello i'm wolfgang puck and today i'm  gonna do a version of a recipe my mother  taught me called kaiserschmann as a kid  in austria we had our own chicken so we  had to go and get the eggs in the bun we  had them really super fresh so the  vanilla bean has seeds inside this is  where all the flavor is but if you can't  get it fresh get a bottle of vanilla i  make kaizajman with my son oliver and  alexander for their mother my wife  so we can serve it to her in bed now if  you're lucky enough you get it served in  bed that's the ultimate  when i grew up in austria we didn't have  electricity in our house and we baked in  a wood burning oven and you know often  now these days we get back to do it  really traditional the old-fashioned way  look at that beautiful egg whites with a  soft peak you see this thing here you  turn it over and it slightly bends over  we want a fluffy and light kaiserschmann  so we're gonna fold in the rest of the  egg whites  you can use any kind of molds you like  the most important thing is though you  have to butter that and sugar that be  sure to have it everywhere the great  thing with kaiserschmann is you can  prepare it in the morning keep it in the  refrigerator and then just cook it at  the last moment now i'm gonna warm up  the strawberries i like strawberries but  in austria we don't have a lot of  strawberries maybe for one month so we  use a lot of plums my mother used to  make plum compote with a little orange  juice or little lemon juice and served  it without kaiserschmidt see how nice  and fluffy our  man  is here perfect  if you make that for mother's day your  mother will feel like a queen it is so  delicious so happy mother's day to all  the mothers around the world  oh yes
 

